WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
Every day, people judge some
acts right and others wrong.

2
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.850
But in this life, goodness and
happiness often fail to match.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.130
The good suffer.

4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.100
The wicked prosper.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.570
In 1788, the philosopher Immanuel Kant
asked what this mismatch means for the

6
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.980
moral life.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:24.380
So if doing right often goes unrewarded,
does morality itself demand that God

8
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.830
exists?

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.360
In this mission, you'll meet two different
kinds of moral argument for God's existence.

10
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.180
Then you'll test them against critics who
say our sense of duty comes from human

11
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.430
sources.

12
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: weigh up whether
unrewarded goodness points to God.
